message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying article and this software release."
title: "Explainable Older ICU Delirium Prediction and Transportability"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/renjingzhuo-maker/older-icu-delirium-transportability"
authors:
  - family-names: Ren
    given-names: Jingzhuo
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Qiannan
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Lixin
  - family-names: Xue
    given-names: Zhaoping
abstract: >-
  Reproducible SQL, Python, R, and PowerShell code for development in MIMIC-IV
  and external evaluation in eICU-CRD of an explainable first-24-hour model
  for late or persistent delirium in serially assessed older intensive care
  patients, including hierarchical external uncertainty, assessment-selection
  analysis, hospital heterogeneity, alternative endpoints, and subgroup
  diagnostics.
keywords:
  - delirium
  - intensive care
  - machine learning
  - external validation
  - transportability
  - MIMIC-IV
  - eICU-CRD
